FILED s543m (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27), from the reviewing session's review of s543m (F5).  PRE-EXISTING: base 9a3ce86f the same.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 | ./runpcl; scratch/s543m/p11/rows.pl prog 5):
    my $f = "/tmp/x.$$"; sub mk { open my $t, ">", $f or die; print $t "hdata"; $t } sub sz { my $s = -s $f; unlink $f; $s // "none" }
    my %h; sub take { delete $h{fh} } $h{fh} = mk(); print { take() } "x"; print "a ", sz(), "\n";
    $h{fh} = mk(); my $cnt = () = take(); print "b ", sz(), " $cnt\n";
perl: a 6 / b 5 1.  PCL (base and tree): a 0 / b 0 1.

SAME PLACE? NO: no statement shape names the drop (the value is consumed by the statement and released at its end: perl's FREETMPS).  A flush there would need a per-statement temporaries notion the drop flush does not have; the s543m `:tail` wrap flushes only in a VOID caller, and here the caller uses the value (as the print's handle / as the countof list).  Left as a residue (ns-escaping-filehandle names it).
